      "math_academy_id": "e-17532",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z,w) = xyzw,$ compute $\\nabla_{x,w} \\: f.$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute $\\nabla_{x,w} \\: f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $x$ and $w$ only.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyzw) & =yzw \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂w}=\\frac{∂}{∂w}(xyzw) & =xyz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,w}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂w}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}yzw \\\\ xyz\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
